sts on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Matt Van Epps (R) is running."]}, "overview": "TN-07, anchored by Nashville's southern suburbs and the Clarksville area, leans Republican by eleven points, and first-term Representative Matt Van Epps is seeking re-election against Democrat Darden Copeland and two minor independents. Rating outlets are nearly unanimous: nine of ten call the race Solid or Safe Republican, with only The Economist at Likely Republican, and prediction markets price a Van Epps win around 97%.\n\nCopeland has still assembled a credible campaign, raising over $1.1 million, and outside groups have spent roughly $2.5 million backing Van Epps against $1.7 million opposing him, signs both sides see some opening. An ethics complaint accusing Van Epps of misusing taxpayer-funded staff has handed Democrats an attack line, and a midterm environment tilted toward the opposition could narrow the margin. With no public polling showing a contest, though, Van Epps remains a clear favorite to hold the seat.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0399, "margin": -11.34}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0635, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0506, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0512, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0318, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0486, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0413, "margin": -12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.049, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0174, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0197, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0585, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0233, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0232, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0193, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0334, "margin": -12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0457, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08"